    {
      "elements": [
        {
          "startIndex": 4753,
          "endIndex": 4934,
          "textRun": {
            "content": "Looking at the distribution of problems solved, we see that the number of questions solved at least once (Pass@8) increases. This suggests that the harness allows us to improve the ",
            "textStyle": {}
          }
        },
        {
          "startIndex": 4934,
          "endIndex": 4942,
          "textRun": {
            "content": "coverage",
            "textStyle": {}
          }
        },
        {
          "startIndex": 4942,
          "endIndex": 4963,
          "textRun": {
            "content": " of the base model. \n",
            "textStyle": {}
          }
        }
      ],
      "paragraphStyle": {
        "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT",
        "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT"
      }
    },
    {
      "elements": [
        {
          "startIndex": 4963,
          "endIndex": 4964,
          "textRun": {
            "content": "\n",
            "textStyle": {}
          }
        }
      ],
      "paragraphStyle": {
        "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT",
        "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT"
      }
    },
    {
      "elements": [
        {
          "startIndex": 4964,
          "endIndex": 5096,
          "textRun": {
            "content": "However, the variance across rollouts also increases – the number of problems solved successfully in all eight rollouts goes down. \n",
            "textStyle": {}
          }
        }
      ],
      "paragraphStyle": {
        "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT",
        "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT"
      }
    },
    {
      "elements": [
        {
          "startIndex": 5096,
          "endIndex": 5097,
          "textRun": {
            "content": "\n",
            "textStyle": {}
          }
        }
      ],
      "paragraphStyle": {
        "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT",
        "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT"
      }
    },
    {
      "elements": [
        {
          "startIndex": 5097,
          "endIndex": 5522,
          "textRun": {
            "content": "Additionally, increasing model size doesn’t necessarily make harness use more reliable. The harness gives both models (regardless of size) the opportunity to decompose and inspect an image, but benefitting from these operations reliably requires learning how to select useful operations and combine evidence. Therefore, we distinguish the ability of a model to solve a question and its ability to visually decompose images. \n",
            "textStyle": {}
          }
        }
      ],
      "paragraphStyle": {
        "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT",
        "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT"
      }
    },
    {
      "elements": [
        {
          "startIndex": 5522,
          "endIndex": 5523,
          "textRun": {
            "content": "\n",
            "textStyle": {}
          }
        }
      ],
      "paragraphStyle": {
        "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT",
        "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT"
      }
    },
    {
      "elements": [
        {
          "startIndex": 5523,
          "endIndex": 5570,
          "textRun": {
            "content": "A few examples of harness use are shown below:\n",
            "textStyle": {}
          }
        }
      ],
      "paragraphStyle": {
        "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT",
        "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT"
      }
    },
    {
      "elements": [
        {
          "startIndex": 5570,
          "endIndex": 5571,
          "textRun": {
